---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import CaseDeck from '../components/CaseDeck.astro';
import ProofDeck from '../components/ProofDeck.astro';
import DeltaDeck from '../components/DeltaDeck.astro';
import ProductHighlight from '../components/ProductHighlight.astro';
import ProductLink from '../components/ProductLink.astro';
import Layers from '../components/Layers.astro';
import Reach from '../components/Reach.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import { companyCta, companyNav, creedLine, site } from '../config';

// The company's landing page: the promise, the situations the product is built for,
// the six parts as one stack, one turn for each part, and the people it is built for.
// The stack comes before the turns so a reader meets the map before the detail.
---

<Base
  title={`${site.name}: ${site.tagline}`}
  description={site.description}
  nav={companyNav}
  cta={companyCta}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow={creedLine}
    title="Replayable Agentic Computing"
    lede="An insulin pump holds a dose. A drone turns back. A robot stops a line. Later, someone asks why, and the machine answers: what it was asked, what it did, and what limited it. That account sits on the device itself, at the moment it happened. The same record computes what happens next."
    body="We make that answer the default. A spatiotemporal record engine on the machine, and a portable mission control where the operator rewinds and proves. No cloud. No database. The record stays where it was made, from edge sensors to space systems, from factory floors to defense programs."
    fieldReveal="scroll"
    depth
  >
    <a class="btn btn--accent" href={companyCta.href} slot="actions" data-hero-cta>
      {companyCta.label} 
    </a>

    <p class="hero-cta-note" slot="actions">
      Public demos and private beta are on the way.
    </p>
    
  </Hero>

  <section class="reach-band" aria-label="Where the engine runs">
    <div class="wrap">
      <Reach />
    </div>
  </section>

  <CaseDeck />

  <Layers /> 
  
  <Section
    id="partners"
    label="The sale"
    title="What is sold, and to whom"
    lede="The engine goes inside a machine someone else ships; the platform goes to the team that operates it. The buyer is the organization that answers for the machine long after it ships."
  >
    <div class="biz">
      <div>
        <p class="biz__k">What is sold</p>
        <p>The engine as a licence per product, against the bill of materials. The record as an audit report, against liability and compliance. Delta as a subscription per deployment, against operations.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="biz__k">How it is sold</p>
        <p>A firmware team licenses the engine and ships it inside its own system. A partner licenses it once across the systems it delivers. Delta can be bought alone, and gains the engine when the record has to be proved on the machine.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="biz__k">Who buys</p>
        <p>Defense programs, medical device makers, vehicle programs, and energy operators. Three people sign the same answer: the executive who deploys, the operator who runs it, and the compliance officer who clears the market.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="biz__k">When it is the product</p>
        <p>When a question over origin, event, and time has to be answered on the machine, with the link down and inside the memory the chip has. Where the record may leave the device, a database or a cloud already does that.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="biz-note">The EU AI Act requires automatic logging over the life of a high-risk system, and the Cyber Resilience Act keeps a manufacturer answerable after it ships. A machine that carries its own record starts inside both.</p>
  </Section>

  <Section
    id="contact"
    label="Contact"
    title="Building a system that has to answer for itself?"
    lede="Write to us. We are choosing the first design partners now."
    band
  >
    <p><a class="btn btn--accent" href={`mailto:${site.contact}`}>Write to us</a></p>
  </Section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The note is a footnote to the call: who can ask for a demo now, and when the
     rest can. */
  .hero-cta-note {
    flex-basis: 100%;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--fg-3);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .reach-band {
    /* The globe starts behind the end of the promise: the copy is read against it,
       and the two are one scene rather than two stacked blocks. */
    margin-top: clamp(-200px, -17vh, -110px);
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding-block: 4px clamp(40px, 6vh, 80px);
    /* The scene opens wider than the window and settles into it. The part that hangs
       past the edge is never on screen, and clipping it sideways keeps a phone from
       scrolling the whole page to reach it. The vertical bleed is the point, so only
       the horizontal axis is clipped. */
    overflow-x: clip;
  }

  /* The sphere is the scene, so it may use the window rather than the reading column,
     and it holds the right edge while the copy holds the left. */
  .reach-band .wrap {
    max-width: none;
    padding-inline: 0;
  }

  /* A phone has no column to give the globe, so the figure sits below the promise. */
  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .reach-band {
      margin-top: -120px;
    }
  }

  /* The deck has no gap under it, and the link that closes the turn needs one. */
  .hl-close {
    padding-block: clamp(20px, 3vh, 32px) clamp(40px, 6vh, 80px);
  }

  /* The regulation line closes the grid as one more cell, so the sale reads as one
     table rather than a table and a footnote. */
  .biz-note {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-top: 0;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .biz {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--line);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .biz > div {
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 22px 24px;
  }

  .biz p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .biz p + p {
    margin-top: 8px;
    color: var(--fg-2);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .biz__k {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--fg-3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .biz {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
